<http://data.silknow.org/object/dbb8a5d1-b447-38fe-b3a6-2c4e05e7d06d/observation/1>
        a                   crmsci:S4_Observation ;
        ecrm:P2_has_type    <http://data.silknow.org/observation/technical-observation> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note    "Hanging of linen-cotton twill decorated with applique motifs worked with wool and some silk in red, blue, cream, yellow and brown. It has button-hole, detached button-hole, hollie point and padded needlepoint stitches.\n\nThe motifs are representations of human figures and plants. In the centre is a female figure in an elaborate fontange with lappets, holding a child in leading reins by either hand (one child is missing and has been replaced by a flower-head); At the top is a pair of figures in what looks like peasant costume and there is also a black woman in European costume, a dwarf and jokers. The hanging also depicts peacocks, a turkey and sheep.\n\nThe ground is covered with embroidered spots in blue wool, and there is an applied edging of flower-heads in detached needlepoint. The top edge has been cut and the hanging has been lined with linen at a later stage."@en ;
        crmsci:O8_observed  <http://data.silknow.org/object/dbb8a5d1-b447-38fe-b3a6-2c4e05e7d06d> .

